#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078149 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "20b289d4-96a7-5d1b-9714-6afabab4804d" :knowledge-point/title "Further Determining Rates of Change in Geometrical Settings"}] :question/id #uuid "a3234c09-08eb-56f2-8a4c-d6430d38c356" :question/math-academy-id "e-275" :question/problem "A spherical balloon is being inflated so that its volume is increasing. Find the instantaneous rate at which the volume of the balloon is changing with respect to the radius at the moment when the diameter of the balloon is equal to $12\\, \\text{cm}$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/620/Source/Images/038c730db46c27977ecaf5b36ce200bc.png)" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given that the diameter of the balloon is $12\\, \\text{cm}$, its radius is\n\n$$\nr =6\\, \\text{cm}\n$$\n\nNow, we know that the volume of a sphere with radius $r$ is given by\n\n$$\nV= V(r) = \\dfrac{4}{3}\\pi r^3\n$$\n\nTaking the derivative, the rate of change of $V(r)$ with respect to $r$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} V'(r) &= \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d r}\\left(\\dfrac{4}{3}\\pi r^3\\right) \\\\[5pt] & = \\dfrac{4}{3}\\pi (3r^2) \\\\[5pt] &= 4\\pi r^2, \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand evaluating at $r=6$ gives\n\n$$\nV'(6)= 4\\pi (6)^2= 144\\pi\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate at which the volume of the balloon is changing when its diameter is $12\\, \\text{cm}\\,$ is $\\, 144\\pi \\, \\text{cm}^3/\\text{cm}$.\n\n**Note:** We read $\\text{cm}^3/\\text{cm}$ as \"centimeters cubed per centimeter\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078150 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dff5ec0b-1456-5231-94e1-0fc5923d6672" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Rate of Change for a Given Function at a Point"}] :question/id #uuid "3c4f9912-4b08-5e11-8ef6-4e4ee35765c7" :question/math-academy-id "e-276" :question/problem "Lizzie buys $b$ pounds of bananas at a price $p$, in dollars, that can be modeled by the function $p(b)=5e^{-0.2b}$. What is the instantaneous rate of change of the price when $b=5$ pounds?" :question/worked-solution "The instantaneous rate of change of the price when $b=5$ pounds is equal to $p'(5)$.\n\nFirst, we take the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\np^{′}(b) &= \\frac{d}{db}(5e^{-0.2b}) \\\\\n&= 5e^{-0.2b} \\cdot (-0.2) \\\\\n&=-e^{-0.2b}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $b=5$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\np^{′}(5) &= -e^{-0.2(5)} \\\\\n&=-e^{-1} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{e}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate change of the price when $b=5$ pounds is\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{1}{e}\n$$\n\ndollars per pound."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078251 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "236cec41-4836-5526-893d-e6f2a23d1801" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Rate of Change for a Given Function"}] :question/id #uuid "f2eda994-e00a-5e9b-a26d-720d01e6fa07" :question/math-academy-id "e-6174" :question/problem "A particle moves in a straight line. After $t$ seconds the particle is $\\, f(t)=2t^3 - 5t + 9\\,$ feet away from its initial position. What is the instantaneous rate of change of the particle's position as a function of $t$?" :question/worked-solution "The instantaneous rate of change of the particle's position is equal to $f'(t)$.\n\nWe take the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{′}(t) &= \\frac{d}{dt}(2t^{3} - 5t + 9) \\\\\n&= 6t^{2} - 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $t$ seconds, the instantaneous rate of change of the particle's position is $6t^2 - 5$ feet per second."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262277 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dff5ec0b-1456-5231-94e1-0fc5923d6672" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Rate of Change for a Given Function at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8870a406-8412-5751-b14a-5f7961b137c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ pounds per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262279} {:answer/id #uuid "8fb54627-a2fe-53a7-8424-00b9cc09f24a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$10$ pounds per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262280} {:answer/id #uuid "47f8fa86-94c2-57b4-a020-597ffe2519df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$15$ pounds per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262281} {:answer/id #uuid "dd113f46-4b31-5b41-bad2-d251fbd9afae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ pounds per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262282} {:answer/id #uuid "265e5f09-9052-5578-afb6-fc447db085b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$7$ pounds per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262283}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8fb54627-a2fe-53a7-8424-00b9cc09f24a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$10$ pounds per year" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262280} :answer-field/id #uuid "569cc057-bc84-5009-b10e-ba39b9d6c179" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262278}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "105b150c-115a-581d-a5ed-c12e12c6e2a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-2439" :question/problem "The weight $w,$ in pounds, of a baby gorilla $t$ years after birth can be modeled by the function $w(t)=4{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}+15.$ What is the instantaneous rate of change of his weight when $t=1$ year?" :question/worked-solution "The instantaneous rate of change of weight when $t=1$ year is equal to ${w}^{′}(1).$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}+15) \\\\  & =12{t}^{2}-2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $t=1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}^{′}(1) & =12(1)^{2}-2(1) \\\\  & =12-2 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate change of the weight when $t=1$ year is $10$ pounds per year."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262284 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dff5ec0b-1456-5231-94e1-0fc5923d6672" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Rate of Change for a Given Function at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cacd8cb5-9238-502f-9314-081400ee8678" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$14$ feet per second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262286} {:answer/id #uuid "19dcd5e9-a528-5f53-8401-723f3102e1b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$ feet per second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262287} {:answer/id #uuid "09baa327-ca7e-5fd5-bfa5-68d13e65d39a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$16$ feet per second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262288} {:answer/id #uuid "a80084d7-549c-5701-821f-8596e309d18b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$27$ feet per second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262289} {:answer/id #uuid "7e250424-4f2a-5df5-aa00-435d6f055dab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$18$ feet per second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09baa327-ca7e-5fd5-bfa5-68d13e65d39a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$16$ feet per second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262288} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5058cad-a6d2-5186-93b0-037fea9994dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262285}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9f34cdca-0767-505c-ad6b-beadde1398f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-2440" :question/problem "A particle moves in a straight line so that after $t$ seconds it is $p(t)={t}^{3}-11t+9$ feet from its initial position. What is the instantaneous rate of change of the particle's position when $t=3$ seconds?" :question/worked-solution "The instantaneous rate of change of the particle's position when $t=3$ seconds is equal to ${p}^{′}(3).$\n\nFirst, we take the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-11t+9) \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}-11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, substituting $t=3,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}^{′}(3) & =3(3)^{2}-11 \\\\  & =27-11 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate change of the particle's position when $t=3$ seconds is $16$ feet per second."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262291 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "236cec41-4836-5526-893d-e6f2a23d1801" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Rate of Change for a Given Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "541fd7d7-6982-5f2f-9745-ea2e7808bf03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{2t+5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262293} {:answer/id #uuid "ec95733b-0d33-5529-ad85-7dd7f7c2c51e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2t+5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262294}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "541fd7d7-6982-5f2f-9745-ea2e7808bf03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{2t+5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262293} :answer-field/id #uuid "6558ba30-4c8a-5c38-8dba-a9083eb2c752" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262292}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b678523d-2283-522f-b86f-4ebdf18393b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-313352" :question/problem "The ambient temperature in a laboratory varies over time. After $t$ seconds, the temperature (in degrees Celsius) is modeled by\n\n$$\nΘ(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2t+5)+18.\n$$\n\nWhat is the instantaneous rate of change of the temperature as a function of $t?$\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change is\n{{field-1}} degrees Celsius per second." :question/worked-solution "The instantaneous rate of change of the temperature is ${Θ}^{′}(t).$\n\nWe take the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Θ}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{d}{dt}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2t+5)+18] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{2t+5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change of the ambient temperature is $\\frac{2}{2t+5}$ degrees Celsius per second."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262295 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "236cec41-4836-5526-893d-e6f2a23d1801" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Rate of Change for a Given Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81a9e964-3a8a-5978-84b8-cbee3c4ae78d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10^t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262297}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81a9e964-3a8a-5978-84b8-cbee3c4ae78d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10^t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262297} :answer-field/id #uuid "08ca6a17-131f-5149-bf73-e53b90f77f28" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262296}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8cf3f18f-5b4e-59b4-9a80-141299bdc32b" :question/math-academy-id "q-343160" :question/problem "The number of views $V,$ in millions, of a viral video after $t$ days is modeled by $V(t)=\\frac{{10}^{t}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}$ for $0\\le t\\le 6.$ What is the instantaneous rate of change of the number of views as a function of $t?$\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change is\n{{field-1}} views per day." :question/worked-solution "The instantaneous rate of change of the number of views is equal to ${V}^{′}(t).$ \n\nFirst, we take the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{V}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{10}^{t}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{10}^{t}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡10}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡10} \\\\  & ={10}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change of the number of views is ${10}^{t}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262298 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "236cec41-4836-5526-893d-e6f2a23d1801" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Rate of Change for a Given Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17011bf5-8813-572c-b8db-fd204a43fbae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12e^{-2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262300}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17011bf5-8813-572c-b8db-fd204a43fbae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12e^{-2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262300} :answer-field/id #uuid "047c645f-3050-55fa-bba8-3898778ad76e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262299}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "04f190f8-b0ca-50fd-afc4-814a3c316fe0" :question/math-academy-id "q-343161" :question/problem "The function $C(t)=6{e}^{-2t}$ gives the concentration, in milligrams per liter, of a medication in the bloodstream $t$ hours after administration. Find the instantaneous rate of change of the concentration as a function of $t.$\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change of the concentration is\n{{field-1}}\nmilligrams per liter per hour." :question/worked-solution "The instantaneous rate of change of the concentration is equal to ${C}^{′}(t).$\n\nNow, the rate of change of $C(t)$ with respect to $t$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{e}^{-2t}) \\\\  & =6(-2){e}^{-2t} \\\\  & =-12{e}^{-2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change of the concentration is $-12{e}^{-2t}$ milligrams per liter per hour."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262301 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "20b289d4-96a7-5d1b-9714-6afabab4804d" :knowledge-point/title "Further Determining Rates of Change in Geometrical Settings"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb503e3b-bd00-53f1-9498-3d66c0c6d75d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262303} {:answer/id #uuid "dc267a72-1f12-5e44-ac07-7ea51933d449" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262304}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc267a72-1f12-5e44-ac07-7ea51933d449" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262304} :answer-field/id #uuid "6700395d-dcc7-5086-a186-e754b313d392" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262302}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e6e2654a-5b06-5727-b889-b8068e0655c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-343488" :question/problem "The bases of a trapezoid are increasing and the larger base is always three times the smaller base. The height of the trapezoid is $3\\,cm.$ Find the rate of change of the area of the trapezoid with respect to its smaller base $b.$\n\nThe rate of change of the area of the trapezoid with respect to its smaller base is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The area of a trapezoid is given by \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{(B+b)h}{2},\n$$\n\n where $b$ is the smaller base, $B$ is the larger base and $h$ is the height of the trapezoid.\n\nWe are given that $B=3b$ and $h=3,$ so we can express the area $A$ as a function of the base $b$ by substituting $B=3b$ and $h=3$ in the formula above. We get\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{(b+3b)(3)}{2}=6b.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $A(b)$ with respect to $b$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{′}(b) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}b}(6b) \\\\  & =6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}b}(b) \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262305 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "20b289d4-96a7-5d1b-9714-6afabab4804d" :knowledge-point/title "Further Determining Rates of Change in Geometrical Settings"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5ef0793-fcfe-5a86-a983-7d6d08b5b9af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{2\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262307}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5ef0793-fcfe-5a86-a983-7d6d08b5b9af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{2\\pi}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262307} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4389edc-42c9-5ff5-9a82-4f1fd486b205" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262306}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7d1e4fcd-7cd2-516b-a124-a0f04de90c73" :question/math-academy-id "q-343491" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948186/assets/c63dfe563c07b143bdc7cc28ab4d1142bea8c455be31ce924fa310c5e4903305.png)\n\nThe area $A$ of the circular disk above is changing as the circle expands. The circumference and radius of the circle are $C$ and $r,$ respectively. \nFind the rate of change of the area of the circle with respect to its circumference.\n\nThe rate of change of the area of the circle with respect to its circumference $C$ is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The area of a circle is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\pi {r}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the circle.\n\nWe know that $C=2\\pi r,$ so we can express the area $A$ as a function of the circumference $C$ by substituting $r=\\frac{C}{2\\pi }$ into the formula above. We get\n\n$$\nA=\\pi {r}^{2}=\\pi {(\\frac{C}{2\\pi })}^{2}=\\frac{{C}^{2}}{4\\pi }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $A(C)$ with respect to $C$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{′}(C) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}C}(\\frac{{C}^{2}}{4\\pi }) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\pi }\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}C}({C}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\pi }(2C) \\\\  & =\\frac{C}{2\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262308 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "20b289d4-96a7-5d1b-9714-6afabab4804d" :knowledge-point/title "Further Determining Rates of Change in Geometrical Settings"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5785436-cf1f-5158-8c54-edccd93d2c30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262310} {:answer/id #uuid "b75dfa85-a23c-5b8f-9414-d11d295bcd2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi {r}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262311} {:answer/id #uuid "a6abc8f3-6154-5ec0-8d43-d76ae7573582" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi {r}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262312} {:answer/id #uuid "15f613d9-aaf6-5a5c-9d18-db16165e9752" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\pi {r}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262313} {:answer/id #uuid "17e16d7f-97a1-5726-9c8c-ecaba05f1d54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{r}^{2}}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262314}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15f613d9-aaf6-5a5c-9d18-db16165e9752" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\pi {r}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262313} :answer-field/id #uuid "145f7fee-116c-5748-a964-4c69b5e8340d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262309}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b9da3be8-6213-5e5a-b4d1-baa350c7d90b" :question/math-academy-id "q-48715" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948186/assets/4915dc00f10fa5edc911cf9744e99e662b705898b32f16391805c7733b8f89e5.png)\n\nThe volume $V$ of the sphere above is increasing. The radius of the sphere is $r.$ Find the rate of change of the volume of a sphere with respect to its radius." :question/worked-solution "The volume of the sphere is given by \n\n$$\nV=V(r)=\\frac{4}{3}\\pi {r}^{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius of the sphere.\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $V(r)$ with respect to $r$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{V}^{′}(r) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}r}(\\frac{4}{3}\\pi {r}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}r}(\\pi {r}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot 3\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =4\\pi {r}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262315 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "236cec41-4836-5526-893d-e6f2a23d1801" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Rate of Change for a Given Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "426c8adb-a5b5-5c02-988a-1a63e3d80136" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$s(\\operatorname{ln}⁡s+2)$ squared millimeters per centimeter" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262317} {:answer/id #uuid "9339905b-5c41-59ae-b1b2-46a86b0d3058" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2\\operatorname{ln}⁡s+1$ squared millimeters per centimeter" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262318} {:answer/id #uuid "b8a34102-0865-5c83-a41a-d820e8889a0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡s$ squared millimeters per centimeter" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262319} {:answer/id #uuid "fdd3244c-a0a0-5c88-bcb4-5872c40df7f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$s(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡s+1)$ squared millimeters per centimeter" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262320} {:answer/id #uuid "3ac030bf-d209-5cc9-83da-88109f66b52e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${s}^{2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡s-1)$ squared millimeters per centimeter" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262321}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fdd3244c-a0a0-5c88-bcb4-5872c40df7f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$s(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡s+1)$ squared millimeters per centimeter" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262320} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e7c9d67-6032-5733-b728-8bfef8996e77" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262316}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "32646f68-3349-52fa-be3e-4f5c20ecb8ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-48716" :question/problem "The function $L(s)={s}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡s$ models the surface area of a flower's petal, in squared millimeters, as the flower's stem grows to a length of $s$ centimeters, where $s>1.$ What is the instantaneous rate of change of the surface area as a function of $s?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}({s}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡s) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}({s}^{2})\\operatorname{ln}⁡s+{s}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡s) \\\\  & =(2s)\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡s+{s}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{s}) \\\\  & =2s\\operatorname{ln}⁡s+s \\\\  & =s(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡s+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate change of the surface area is $s(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡s+1)$ squared millimeters per centimeter."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262322 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "20b289d4-96a7-5d1b-9714-6afabab4804d" :knowledge-point/title "Further Determining Rates of Change in Geometrical Settings"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "793e2126-ee2e-507f-8e8f-3047f3ee0415" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262324} {:answer/id #uuid "e0487cbf-9e86-5200-b92d-2893b59f2778" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}/\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262325} {:answer/id #uuid "29941a62-a075-51e5-97c6-0e2aa7f969a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}/\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262326} {:answer/id #uuid "fdedc5d1-9be8-57bd-920d-21e25bb00022" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262327} {:answer/id #uuid "ddff0772-8081-50bd-bdf9-7468b4f7f3cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}/\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262328}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29941a62-a075-51e5-97c6-0e2aa7f969a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}/\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262326} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b70f361-4268-5e3f-81d5-197dd437dd57" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262323}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9ae90c2c-65ba-5cd2-9c97-71c571033581" :question/math-academy-id "q-48720" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948186/assets/2b5d589462bf2477be3d305ea88f3d5462b7d6ea4e001a9a71790d53e1683665.png)\n\nThe area of a square is increasing. Find the instantaneous rate at which the area of a square is increasing with respect to the length of its side at the moment when the length of the sides is equal to $l=6\\,\\text{cm}.$" :question/worked-solution "We know that the area of the square with respect to $l$ is given by  \n\n$$\nA=A(l)={l}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTaking the derivative, the rate of change of $A(l)$  with respect to $l$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{′}(l) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}l}({l}^{2})=2l,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand evaluating at $l=6$ gives\n\n$$\n{A}^{′}(6)=2(6)=12.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate at which the area of the square is increasing when the length of the side is $l=6\\,\\text{cm}$ is $12\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}/\\text{cm}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078941 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "20b289d4-96a7-5d1b-9714-6afabab4804d" :knowledge-point/title "Further Determining Rates of Change in Geometrical Settings"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8bd2b21f-a739-5a2c-8947-9ffb1b500757" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076858} {:answer/id #uuid "cd3bf12f-57b3-53a2-931e-981a627ea615" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076859} {:answer/id #uuid "e6965292-1b93-5b27-bc2a-5045c54beefe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076860} {:answer/id #uuid "356f9d42-a444-5e88-ade0-fa7121a66ef3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10b^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076861} {:answer/id #uuid "7c1baaff-d2e6-57b8-91d3-b512f6cf233c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076862}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6965292-1b93-5b27-bc2a-5045c54beefe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076860} :answer-field/id #uuid "882f7b55-1931-5130-b0d2-4f536cda651a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186076857}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6f5c7d68-86e4-553b-96a2-1701e7dfe5af" :question/math-academy-id "q-48725" :question/problem "The area of the rectangle is increasing. The base of the rectangle is $b$, and its height is $10$ times its base. Find the rate of change of the area of a rectangle with respect to its base." :question/worked-solution "The area of a rectangle is given by  \n\n$$\nA=bh,\n$$\n\n where $b$ is the base and $h$ is the height of the rectangle.\n\nWe are given that $h=10b,$ so we can express the area $A$ as a function of the base $b$ by substituting $h=10b$ in the formula above. We get\n\n$$\nA=b(10b)=10{b}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $A(b)$  with respect to $b$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{′}(b) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}b}(10{b}^{2}) \\\\  & =10\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}b}({b}^{2}) \\\\  & =10(2b) \\\\  & =20b.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262329 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dff5ec0b-1456-5231-94e1-0fc5923d6672" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Rate of Change for a Given Function at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5a9fcf4-cb9b-5f03-b7fe-30629a356cb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\frac{4}{3}$ dollars per gallon" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262331} {:answer/id #uuid "970f8a8e-ae8d-5083-9796-939275e798f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\frac{3}{4}$ dollars per gallon" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262332} {:answer/id #uuid "637f4574-bbd3-5b60-a12e-f4585452c817" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\frac{3}{4}$ gallons per dollar" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262333} {:answer/id #uuid "5d2e8223-aa73-5fdf-b1c8-a06201a1ea66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\frac{1}{3}$ dollars per gallon" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262334} {:answer/id #uuid "d81dde64-6e4e-5f3c-81b1-edc328a772aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\frac{4}{3}$ gallons per dollar" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262335}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5a9fcf4-cb9b-5f03-b7fe-30629a356cb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-\\frac{4}{3}$ dollars per gallon" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262331} :answer-field/id #uuid "4bed608d-f02e-5aeb-a964-2ac240b404ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262330}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9aa60056-cf3e-58e8-bae0-fd58cc5adfa3" :question/math-academy-id "q-48742" :question/problem "The function $P(v)=\\frac{2v+50}{v+1}$ models the price at which gas is sold, in dollars, depending on the volume $v$ sold the previous day, in gallons. What is the instantaneous rate of change of the price of gas when $v=5$ gallons?" :question/worked-solution "The instantaneous rate of change of the price when $v=5$ gallons is equal to ${P}^{′}(5).$\n\nNow, we take the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{′}(v) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}v}(\\frac{2v+50}{v+1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}v}(2v+50)\\cdot (v+1)-(2v+50)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}v}(v+1)}{(v+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2)\\cdot (v+1)-(2v+50)\\cdot (1)}{(v+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2v+2-2v-50}{(v+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{48}{(v+1)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $v=5$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{′}(5) & =-\\frac{48}{((5)+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{48}{36} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate change of the price when $v=5$ gallons is $-\\frac{4}{3}$ dollars per gallon."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262336 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dff5ec0b-1456-5231-94e1-0fc5923d6672" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Rate of Change for a Given Function at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff3ea3a0-0252-57e3-aeec-232b99135da4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$ meters per second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262338} {:answer/id #uuid "96f05212-4e3a-599e-92ef-43d04918b0f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$ meter per second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262339} {:answer/id #uuid "1e3f02ef-59c7-5837-a6c2-9d92c02c90d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ meters per second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262340} {:answer/id #uuid "b8fb16e8-cf8a-5273-9f9e-97b4fbe73eba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ meters per second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262341} {:answer/id #uuid "0445507a-2423-5178-bf12-706b5c412c22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$ meters per second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262342}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff3ea3a0-0252-57e3-aeec-232b99135da4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$ meters per second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262338} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e1d0e37-098a-5943-85a3-515d49a429e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262337}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2e527e4e-1ea7-5d39-a401-6a8d7982a17f" :question/math-academy-id "q-72352" :question/problem "The function $x(t)={t}^{2}+t$ models the distance traveled by a car $t$ seconds after it sets off on a journey. Find the instantaneous rate at which the distance traveled by the car is changing with respect to time when $t=1$ second." :question/worked-solution "The instantaneous rate at which the distance traveled by the car is changing when $t=1$ second is equal to ${x}^{′}(1).$\n\nTaking the derivative, the rate of change of $x(t)$ with respect to $t$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+t)=2t+1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand evaluating at $t=1$ gives\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(1)=2(1)+1=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate at which the distance traveled by the car is changing when $t=1$ second is $3$ meters per second."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262343 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dff5ec0b-1456-5231-94e1-0fc5923d6672" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Rate of Change for a Given Function at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5a47853-b09d-5433-ac5d-3e6ed2b7945e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\frac{11}{8}$ cubic centimeters per second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262345} {:answer/id #uuid "cb3273a8-5ad5-5ef4-b480-ff5dca96b779" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\frac{7}{8}$ cubic centimeters per second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262346} {:answer/id #uuid "6191f350-adf2-5192-8d13-f3556935fdd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\frac{7}{16}$ cubic centimeters per second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262347} {:answer/id #uuid "2c148a25-b71b-5184-a328-e2b08a144dca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\frac{7\\sqrt{30}}{60}$ cubic centimeters per second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262348} {:answer/id #uuid "a98ba616-2146-5601-8995-23f7f9943b16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\frac{11}{16}$ cubic centimeters per second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb3273a8-5ad5-5ef4-b480-ff5dca96b779" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\frac{7}{8}$ cubic centimeters per second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262346} :answer-field/id #uuid "13329ba6-19a3-5419-817c-1900d14a9f79" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262344}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "072688e5-9941-5223-b2ce-40292e03ba47" :question/math-academy-id "q-72358" :question/problem "The volume $V$ (in cubic centimeters) of water in a pail $s$ seconds after it starts filling can be modeled by the function $V(s)=7\\sqrt{s}+2.$ Find the instantaneous rate at which the volume of water is changing with respect to time at the moment when the volume of water in the pail is equal to $30$ cubic centimeters." :question/worked-solution "Since we are given that the volume of water in the pail is $30$ cubic centimeters, the time can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}30 & =7\\sqrt{s}+2 \\\\ 7\\sqrt{s} & =28 \\\\ \\sqrt{s} & =4 \\\\ s & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe instantaneous rate at which the volume of water in the pail is changing when $s=16$ seconds is equal to ${V}^{′}(16).$\n\nTaking the derivative, the rate of change of $V(s)$ with respect to $s$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{V}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(7\\sqrt{s}+2) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(7{s}^{1/2}+2) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}{s}^{-1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{s}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand evaluating at $s=16$ gives\n\n$$\n{V}^{′}(16)=\\frac{7}{2\\sqrt{16}}=\\frac{7}{8}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate at which the volume of water in the pail is changing when $s=16$ seconds is $\\frac{7}{8}$ cubic centimeters per second."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262350 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "236cec41-4836-5526-893d-e6f2a23d1801" :knowledge-point/title "Determining a Rate of Change for a Given Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a52c4689-da7a-570e-8989-65b6edf76e48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\frac{710}{1+{e}^{-t}}$  liters per day" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262352} {:answer/id #uuid "27d04d21-825b-59ef-bea0-e7136ff9cae3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\frac{355}{1+{e}^{-t}}$ liters per day" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262353} {:answer/id #uuid "f9b91f08-9fb4-5b3f-9b4a-1814f2033caf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$355{e}^{t}$  liters per day" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262354} {:answer/id #uuid "db14086d-d818-5ca4-a619-9770d3a947e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\frac{710{e}^{t}}{2+{e}^{-t}}$  liters per day" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262355} {:answer/id #uuid "43741ee7-1f7c-5b81-9f09-2b2714183729" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$710{e}^{-t}$  liters per day" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a52c4689-da7a-570e-8989-65b6edf76e48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\frac{710}{1+{e}^{-t}}$  liters per day" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262352} :answer-field/id #uuid "5fde2b24-adb2-54a1-9c8d-6b66f11b4bbd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262351}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e1a7b751-463a-5c53-9c04-73eeed9f0b75" :question/math-academy-id "q-86191" :question/problem "The function $P(t)=710\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{e}^{t})$ represents the volume of milk, in liters, produced on a farm $t$ days after the owner bought new cows. What is the instantaneous rate of change of the volume of produced milk as a function of $t?$" :question/worked-solution "The instantaneous rate of change of the volume of produced milk with respect to time is ${P}^{′}(t).$\n\nNow, the rate of change of $P(t)$ with respect to $t$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(710\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{e}^{t})) \\\\  & =710\\,\\frac{{e}^{t}}{1+{e}^{t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{710}{1+{e}^{-t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change of the volume of produced milk is  $\\frac{710}{1+{e}^{-t}}$ liters per day."}]}
